WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.090
Recently, I went to a circus festival.

2
00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:06.730
There was a huge circus tent.

3
00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:09.370
And many different circus performers.

4
00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:13.050
It was a celebration of circus arts!

5
00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:14.610
That looks fun, Anna.

6
00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:18.230
But I don’t think circus performers are artists.

7
00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:23.330
I think they’re athletes with interesting skills … and costumes.

8
00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:27.010
Hmm, that is a very interesting point of view, Pete.

9
00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:29.430
And I completely disagree.

10
00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:33.430
Anna, Michelangelo was an artist.

11
00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:36.090
Rembrandt was an artist.

12
00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:39.870
People who swing from ropes are not artists.

13
00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:44.670
I know it’s not easy to swing from a bar and catch someone by the hands.

14
00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:47.670
You have to be very athletic to do that.

15
00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:48.950
That’s a good point, Pete.

16
00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:50.950
They are athletic.

17
00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:54.770
But they are called trapeze artists.

18
00:00:56.060 --> 00:00:57.410
Trapeze … ARTISTS.

19
00:00:57.960 --> 00:00:59.850
I hear what you’re saying, Anna.

20
00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:00.390
I do.

21
00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:03.090
But where is the art?

22
00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:04.430
Look at these guys.

23
00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:06.290
They’re jugglers.

24
00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:10.710
Yes, they are skilled in the art of juggling.

25
00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:12.530
They have a special skill.

26
00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:13.930
But are they artists?

27
00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:14.530
Yes!

28
00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:14.790
No!

29
00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:17.810
They're just throwing things back and forth.

30
00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:19.310
Kind of like you and me, Pete.

31
00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:21.870
We’re going back and forth on this issue.

32
00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:26.050
I don’t think we’ll ever agree on this one.

33
00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:31.330
No, but we can agree that these young people are amazing.

34
00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:33.110
Okay, yeah.

35
00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:35.030
We can agree on that.

36
00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:40.570
But, still, they are very athletic – flipping and throwing each other around.

37
00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:43.350
Yes, I agree with you on that point.

38
00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:44.750
They did it!

39
00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:45.050
They agreed!!

40
00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:49.590
Anna says she agrees that the performers are athletic.

41
00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:51.570
“That’s a good point, Pete.

42
00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:53.550
They are athletic.

43
00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:55.750
I agree with you on that point.”

44
00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:58.750
Now look for other ways they agree.

45
00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:00.510
Anna?

46
00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:02.470
Anna!!

47
00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:05.250
Sorry! Sorry!

48
00:02:05.420 --> 00:02:07.030
But he’s an artist too.

49
00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:11.590
He is telling a story with his sticks and his costume.

50
00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:12.710
What story?

51
00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:14.590
What costume?

52
00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:16.990
I see your point, Pete.

53
00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:18.430
I really do.

54
00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:22.330
But circus performers do more than physical tricks.

55
00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:23.270
Look!

56
00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:25.410
Look at these amazing performers!

57
00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:29.970
I will admit -- I like their costumes.

58
00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:31.030
You know, Pete.

59
00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:34.990
Let’s let the performers speak for themselves.

60
00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:41.030
Kate and Piper tell stories while hanging upside down on a ring!

61
00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:44.470
Was it hard to interview them upside down?

62
00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:47.210
I interviewed them right side up, Pete.

63
00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:53.670
Kate says circus performing may be athletic but it’s not competitive.

64
00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:56.670
With most sports, you compete.

65
00:02:56.840 --> 00:02:59.490
It’s an art form because like, other sports are competing.

66
00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:01.810
This is simply performing and having fun.
